# 5. Project Planning

## 5.1 Project Work Plans

The provided SRS does not specify a detailed work breakdown structure or individual team work plan.

Based on the system requirements documented in the SRS, implementation work can be organized around:
- User registration and verification.
- Authentication.
- Receiver verification.
- Data upload and form creation.
- Redaction and preview.
- Watermarking.
- Encryption and secure transmission.
- Access-control management.
- Receiver data viewing.
- Access requests.
- Activity logging.
- Notifications.
- Temporary storage and automatic deletion.

## 5.2 Work Activities

### Authentication and User Management
- Register user accounts.
- Verify email addresses.
- Authenticate users.
- Manage verified-user access.

### Secure Data Sharing
- Verify receiver identity.
- Select image or form sharing mode.
- Upload or create data.
- Apply redaction.
- Preview shared data.
- Set access controls.
- Encrypt and transmit data.

### Access Management
- Set expiry time.
- Set view limits.
- Configure resharing permissions.
- Modify permissions.
- Revoke access.
- Re-grant access.

### Receiver Operations
- Receive notifications.
- View shared data.
- Request additional access.
- Request reveal of marked/redacted areas.
- View updated data after approval.

### Monitoring and Security
- Track access activity.
- Record audit logs.
- Send notifications.
- Apply watermarks.
- Enforce expiry and view limits.
- Delete expired data.

